abstract: >-
  An end-to-end open-source framework that derives SUMO network geometry,
  vehicle demand, and signal phase data entirely from fixed-infrastructure
  LiDAR and roadside unit deployments, requiring no manual network editing
  and no OpenStreetMap import. The framework extracts per-vehicle
  trajectories, validates them against camera ground truth, replays them in
  SUMO at full sensor resolution, and computes per-vehicle delay, stopped
  delay, queue length, and throughput per signal cycle. Validated across six
  30-minute recordings spanning peak, off-peak, and overnight conditions at a
  four-approach signalized intersection.
